   "notes": "Emmanuel College range on St Andrew's Street north of the Essex front, seen over the boundary wall and railings. Two parts: northern ~10 m rendered (pale pink/buff) with a row of six small upper windows and a chimney; southern ~21 m ashlar with three gabled bays rising through the copper-green roof, each with a pair of tall mullioned-and-transomed windows. Ground-floor openings hidden behind the boundary wall, not annotated. Positions scaled from oblique Geograph views."
